==[[Toon of the Week]] Quests==
{{TOTWQuests|Encounter {{CI|Twisted Finn|name=true}} 3 times.|Encounter the [[Ichor Leak]] Event while playing as Finn.|Complete 10 [[Machines]] in a run with the {{TI|Fishing Rod|name=true}} [[Trinket]] equipped.}}

===Rewards===
*1 Quest completed: {{AT|Finn Fan}} [[Title]]
*2 Quests completed: {{SI|Golden Finn!|name=true}} [[Sticker]]
*3 Quests completed: {{Skin|Golden Fishbowl|toon=Finn}} [[Skin]]

===Strategies===
*For the first Quest, it is recommended to just play normally, as {{Type|Uncommon}} [[Twisteds]] like him are still fairly common on the early Floors. However, when you reach a high Floor like 25, it is recommended to restart, as Uncommons get rarer the farther you go. This can also be done with {{CI|Twisted Finn|name=true}} on the [[Daily Twisted Board]].
*For the second Quest, play normally as Finn, but skip out on the {{CDI|Piping Tape|name=true}} and pick {{CDI|Electrician|name=false}}, giving you the highest chance of an [[Ichor Leak]].
*For the third Quest, alongside {{TI|Fishing Rod|name=true}}, it is recommended to use a speed boosting Trinket like {{TI|Pull Toy|name=true}} or having a [[Toon]] speed you up when a [[Floor]] starts, like {{CI|Tisha|name=true}}. This can help you reach [[Machines]] quickly. You can also use extraction boosting Trinkets like {{TI|Vee's Remote|name=true}} to be able to extract more Machines. With how Fishing Rod synergizes with this Quest, it should be done quickly. It can be more easy in a solo run, as you'll have dibs on all Machines, you’ll only need to reach Floor 4 to extract 10 Machines if you choose to do this instead.

==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.
*For the second requirement, you can go into multiple runs and do as many machines as you can. To do this, focus on using a [[Toon]] that has a fast Extraction Speed or Big Skill Check, You can also use trinkets that increase your Skill Check or Extraction.

==Strategies==
Finn is a beginner friendly [[Toon]] that serves greatly for those who want to practice their skills if they struggle with extracting, whilst also providing great escapability with his Passive [[Ability]], '''Reel In'''. His Passive Ability can help with his main weaknesses, average speed and subpar [[Stamina]], gaining a 35% [[Movement Speed]] increase for 10 seconds, every time a [[Machine]] is completed. This makes it a great survival tool for him given the amazing speeds it gives when multiple Machines are finished at once, with 4 Machines completed allowing him to outwalk {{CI|Twisted Dyle|name=true}} outside of [[Panic Mode]]. To see these speeds in full for every Machine that can be possibly finished at a time, see the table below.
{{SFSpeedTable|Finn}}

While his Passive Ability is active, [[Twisteds]] such as {{CI|Twisted Vee|name=true}} (normally lowers speed by -25%, fully countered to a 1.2% speed boost while Ability is active) are reduced threats. [[Ichor Leaks]] can also be less of an issue, as walking through Ichor Puddles won't be as dangerous (normally lowers speed by -15%, fully countered with a 14.7% speed boost).

Since Finn will always receive a speed boost during Panic Mode, it's a good idea to preserve a little Stamina for it. Given that Finn's Stamina is lower than average, choosing the {{CDI|Well-Paced/Endurance|name=true}} cards will provide a significant increase to his strength and allow him to make use of his ability more often, and his above average extractability makes him great for completing {{CDI|TIME'S UP}}[[Dyle's Floor]] with ease. If otherwise unable to do these, prioritizing Stamina Items and managing Stamina by not running as much when not being chased can be great alternatives.

Finn's Passive Ability gives him the potential to be a decent distractor for teams with good extractor Toons, especially in Floors with high Machine counts. However, his less than great Stamina should be noted, alongside with the fact that, even if using {{TI|Speedy Shoes|name=true}} or {{TI|Dog Plush|name=true}}, Finn is unable to out-walk most of the Twisteds in the game unless the Machine completion is timed correctly, so only distract as him as a backup distractor or use better Toons that are more fit for the role. He can still help other Toons make it to the [[Elevator]] in [[Panic Mode]] due to his buff when the last Machine is completed, and can distract the Twisteds that are near the Elevator until all the Toons have made it in.

Overall, Finn is a great survivalist and extractor, in spite of his lower Stamina, his Ability helps remedy it. He's a very good Toon in teams, due to the increased opportunities for Ability activation, though he has a fair potential in solo runs.

