==Trivia==
*In Finn's head lies {{CI|Barnaby Wilikers|name=true}}, a purple-striped plastic wind-up fish toy, visible in his Idle animation quirk and his current extraction animation.
**Currently, only him and [[Blot]] have a [[Minor Character]] ''with'' them, them being Barnaby Wilikers and {{CI|Blot Jr.|name=true}}, respectively.
***They are paired together in their own [[Stickers]].
***Similarly to Blot Jr., Barnaby's [[Skin]] changes in some of Finn's Skins.
**This makes Finn the first [[Toon]] capable of carrying an object and/or a Toon in their head, with the second being {{CI|Gigi|name=true}} and the third being {{CI|Bassie|name=true}}.
**According to {{CI|Dandy|name=true}} in a [[gossip]], Barnaby can blink, move suspiciously fluid, and respond to Finn. Dandy himself and {{CI|Gourdy|name=true}} are only Toon that's aware of this. It's also unknown if he appeared in the original [[Show]].
***Barnaby is likely a robot, given the wind key on his neck and since he really can move by himself, while still being framed as a toy at the same time. 
***According to Finn's dialogue with {{CI|Sprout|name=true}}, Finn considers him as "more than just a toy fish", implying that Dandy was completely right.
***One [[Sticker]] shows Barnaby in a thinking pose alongside Finn. While the Sticker isn't part of the lore, it can still show elements of it and therefore ''could'' support Dandy's gossip.
***In an official [https://youtube.com/shorts/o_P_iqzPGrY?si=fu-FYJKsUcP5X9OC video] posted featuring Dandy and Finn, Barnaby can also be seen having a shocked expression for a second when Finn jumps. This might support Dandy's gossip too.
*It is unknown how, when, and why Finn lost his tooth.
*Finn and {{CI|Teagan|name=true}} have some similarities:
**Both were surprise [[Toons]] with no prior promotion and got released in updates with 4 Toons each.
***Coincidentally, both of them also appeared in a thumbnail for the [[Changelog|v0.3]] alongside {{CI|Twisted Goob|name=true}}.
***They were the {{Type|Uncommon}} Toons of their updates.
**Both are the only Toons who have liquids in their heads and have to use a comically large cork while sleeping, due to it being quite funny<ref>https://discordapp.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1300070907372634152</ref> and likely because it makes sense with being cartoon characters, even though they've never been seen doing this at all, not even in the official illustrations.
**They share similar [[Stats]], swapping [[Stamina]], [[Stealth]], and [[Skill Check]].
**They were optimized in v0.13.14.
*Finn's name was likely chosen because Finn sounds very similar to 'fin', a body part most fish have.
*The first line that Finn says in one of his interactions with [[Shrimpo]] may be a reference to the "Why So Serious" line from Joker in ''The Dark Knight'', and also the meme of the same name.
*Finn's icon has white buckles on his vest, while his model and Introduction Card artwork have black buckles. This is likely a minor art/coloring mistake.
*Finn drinks exclusively water, as confirmed in an interaction with [[Teagan]].
**This could be Finn worrying drinking any other liquid could contaminate either Barnaby or the liquid inside his head, as possibly implied by his {{CI|Twisted Finn}}[[Twisted Finn|Twisted counterpart]] and his [[Skins]], despite that one of them, being his Flowery Punch skin having fruit punch in his head with no ill effects.
*While walking or running, water can be seen splashing out of Finn's head every few seconds.
**Prior to his optimization, this small particle effect was only visible to the Finn user; no one else could see it.
*The outline effect visible on Finn's head and arms is created by having a blue-colored surface surrounding these parts of him. The surface can only be seen from the inside, so his arms and head are visible through it, but since it is slightly enlarged, some of its inside can be seen surrounding Finn, creating the outline.
**This technique is also used for the outlines on {{CI|Poppy|name=true}}, as well as both Toons' [[Twisted]] counterparts.
*Finn and {{CI|Shelly|name=true}} are very similar, with both having almost the same Passive [[Ability]] (Shelly getting 25% speed while Finn gets 35%) and similar [[Stats]] (Finn lacks 1{{Star}} in Skill Check compared to her). They both also have a topic they specialize and center around, with Finn specializing around marine biology and Shelly around paleontology.
**Ironically, they both remind {{CI|Brightney|name=true}} of something, that being a goldfish and a Troodon.
*Finn talks with all of the base game [[Toons]]; the [[Event Toons]] except [[Bobette]] are all excluded.
*Finn, along with {{CI|Blot|name=true}}, {{CI|Brusha|name=true}}, [[Gigi]], and {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}, is one of the few [[Toons]] to not have a revealed full icon.
*Finn's friends include {{CI|Razzle|name=true}} and possibly [[Shrimpo]].
**In Finn's lore video, Razzle expresses support towards Finn's desire to share more marine life facts, rather than focusing on solely puns and jokes due to {{CI|Arthur|name=true}}'s demand. He also tries to comfort him after noticing his sadness. Razzle also proclaims that Finn is his "best friend", with both of them having some shared enjoyment of comedy.
**Shrimpo's and Finn's possible friendship may be hinted at in a [[Gossip]] with [[Dandy]]. This could also be implied by their matching Christmas [[Skins]], Ice Fisher and Bundled Up, respectively.
**Finn is the first Toon to not mind [[Shrimpo]]'s bullying and responds positively.
*Finn is the third [[Toon]] that was not released during the game's launch to be optimized, with the first two being [[Cosmo]] and [[Sprout]], and the second being [[Glisten]] and [[Shelly]].
**Coincidentally, all of them, except Shelly, released in the same update (v0.3).
***However, since the other three were mentioned in the Welcome To Gardenview poster, before [[Changelog|v0.13.14]], he was also one of the three unoptimized toons to not be featured and any posters during the Launch prior to release, with the other two being [[Gigi]] and [[Teagan]].
*If you enter the [[Aquatic Floor]] map as Finn and go to his section, he will say "{{Text|...I really do miss when these tanks were filled with critters.}}".
**If you approach the Lore Video with Finn and {{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}}, he will say "{{Text|Haha... this isn't so funny.}}".
*The sound used for Finn's '''Reel In''' Ability originates from Flood Escape 2. It is uploaded on the Roblox Audio Library as "[https://create.roblox.com/store/asset/7815311416/Flood-escape-Splash-sound Flood escape Splash sound.wav]".
*Finn is the second [[Toon]] in general and the first non-[[Main]] Toon to have a [[Toon of the Week]]. With this, he is the first non-Main Toon to:
**Have a Golden and Robux-exclusive [[Skin]] while not being [[Event]] exclusive.
**Have a dedicated Lore video.
**Have 2 dialogues in one Floor.
***Finn is the second one to receive dialogue in a map they previously never had dialogue in, with the first being {{CI|Bassie|name=true}}.
**Have their own [[Title]].
***He is also the only Toon to have their own [[Machine]] Type.
*Erroneously, in [[Changelog|v0.23.1]], Finn would have {{TTDI|Barnaby|name=true}}<ref>[[File:TwistedBarnabyinFinn'sFishbowl.png|200px]]</ref> inside his head when working on an arcade machine instead of the regular [[Toon]] counterpart due to a bug.

